        <type>void</type>
        <definition>void LiveIntervalCalc::extendToUses</definition>
        <argsstring>(LiveRange &amp;LR, Register Reg, LaneBitmask LaneMask, LiveInterval *LI=nullptr)</argsstring>
        <name>extendToUses</name>
        <qualifiedname>llvm::LiveIntervalCalc::extendToUses</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="classllvm_1_1_live_range" kindref="compound">LiveRange</ref> &amp;</type>
          <declname>LR</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="classllvm_1_1_register" kindref="compound">Register</ref></type>
          <declname>Reg</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="structllvm_1_1_lane_bitmask" kindref="compound">LaneBitmask</ref></type>
          <declname>LaneMask</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="classllvm_1_1_live_interval" kindref="compound">LiveInterval</ref> *</type>
          <declname>LI</declname>
          <defval>nullptr</defval>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Extend the live range of <computeroutput>LR</computeroutput> to reach all uses of Reg. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>If <computeroutput>LR</computeroutput> is a main range, or if <computeroutput>LI</computeroutput> is null, then all uses must be jointly dominated by the definitions from <computeroutput>LR</computeroutput>. If <computeroutput>LR</computeroutput> is a subrange of the live interval <computeroutput>LI</computeroutput>, corresponding to lane mask <computeroutput>LaneMask</computeroutput>, all uses must be jointly dominated by the definitions from <computeroutput>LR</computeroutput> together with definitions of other lanes where <computeroutput>LR</computeroutput> becomes undefined (via &lt;def,read-undef&gt; operands). If <computeroutput>LR</computeroutput> is a main range, the <computeroutput>LaneMask</computeroutput> should be set to ~0, i.e. <ref refid="structllvm_1_1_lane_bitmask_1a3714a639930eab71d7202da05ad82990" kindref="member">LaneBitmask::getAll()</ref>. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="include/llvm/CodeGen/LiveIntervalCalc.h" line="39" column="8" bodyfile="lib/CodeGen/LiveIntervalCalc.cpp" bodystart="134" bodyend="194"/>
      </memberdef>
    </sectiondef>
